title: NikoEventStart
---
<<declare $playerName = "">>
<<gathervars>>
Recalling what happened through the haze of your pounding head was
a struggle. Like any other day, it started with your routine.

Wake up, breakfast, ride the bus...

You were heading to class when something sharp struck your head.

You tried to reach back, but felt nothing. Your body was numb.

A faint tingling spread beneath your skin.

Panic struck as you realized you couldn’t see.

Slowly, your senses returned. A fabric was tied over your eyes.

Feeling returned to your body. You weren’t paralyzed, just bound.

Plastic bit into your wrists as you struggled. Zip ties, likely.

Panic rose into a choked sob. You were bound, bruised, terrified.

You tried to scream, but your mouth was gagged with silk.

<<set $NikoDiaImage = true>>
Niko: "You asked me yesterday, 'Should one outweigh many?'"
<<set $NikoDiaImage = false>>

<<set $NikoDiaImage = true>>
Niko: "Do you remember that?"
<<set $NikoDiaImage = false>>

<<set $NikoDiaImage = true>>
Niko: "It got me thinking... you agreed with me."
<<set $NikoDiaImage = false>>

<<set $NikoDiaImage = true>>
Niko: "So I was foolish not to act on it."
<<set $NikoDiaImage = false>>

<<set $NikoDiaImage = true>>
Niko: "Why let this opportunity slip through my fingers?"
<<set $NikoDiaImage = false>>

Hands loosened the blindfold.

<<set $NikoDiaImage = true>>
Niko: "There. Isn't it good to see again?"
<<set $NikoDiaImage = false>>

You recognized the voice immediately.

Niko.

<<set $NikoDiaImage = true>>
Niko: "Ah-ah. No noise."
<<set $NikoDiaImage = false>>

<<set $NikoDiaImage = true>>
Niko: "We wouldn't want anyone finding you."
<<set $NikoDiaImage = false>>

-> Muffled Scream
    <<jump NEchoice1>>
-> Headbutt him
    <<incRelationship "Niko" 1>>
    <<jump NEchoice2>>
-> Accept
    <<decRelationship "Niko" 1>>
    <<jump NEchoice3>>
===

title: NEchoice1
---
You screamed into the gag, hoping it wasn’t as muffled as he claimed.

<<jump NE2>>
===

title: NEchoice2
---
<<gathervars>>
Your head slammed into his nose.

Blood spilled instantly.

<<set $NikoDiaImage = true>>
Niko: "You fucking brat!"
<<set $NikoDiaImage = false>>

<<set $NikoDiaImage = true>>
Niko: "All I want is for us to be together."
<<set $NikoDiaImage = false>>

<<set $NikoDiaImage = true>>
Niko: "Don't you want that?"
<<set $NikoDiaImage = false>>

You shook your head violently.

<<jump NE2>>
===

title: NEchoice3
---
<<gathervars>>
You lowered your head in acceptance.

What was the point in fighting?

You were tired.

Exams. Essays. Everything.

But you also hated losing control.

<<jump NE2>>
===

title: NE2
---
<<gathervars>>
Niko’s expression darkened.

<<set $NikoDiaImage = true>>
Niko: "It would be easier if you stopped resisting."
<<set $NikoDiaImage = false>>

<<set $NikoDiaImage = true>>
Niko: "This is your life now."
<<set $NikoDiaImage = false>>

<<set $NikoDiaImage = true>>
Niko: "My happiness matters more. You agreed!"
<<set $NikoDiaImage = false>>

<<set $NikoDiaImage = true>>
Niko: "You agreed!"
<<set $NikoDiaImage = false>>

He struck a vase. It shattered.

Glass scattered. Blood dripped from his hand.

<<set $NikoDiaImage = true>>
Niko: "Now look what you made me do."
<<set $NikoDiaImage = false>>

<<set $NikoDiaImage = true>>
Niko: "It's alright."
<<set $NikoDiaImage = false>>

<<set $NikoDiaImage = true>>
Niko: "I forgive you."
<<set $NikoDiaImage = false>>

He adjusted your shirt.

<<set $NikoDiaImage = true>>
Niko: "Always look your best for your love."
<<set $NikoDiaImage = false>>

<<set $NikoDiaImage = true>>
Niko: "It's okay. It's okay."
<<set $NikoDiaImage = false>>

His amber eyes locked onto yours.

<<set $NikoDiaImage = true>>
Niko: "We'll be together forever now."
<<set $NikoDiaImage = false>>

<<set $NikoDiaImage = true>>
Niko: "Won't we?"
<<set $NikoDiaImage = false>>
<<determineNikoEnd>>
===

title: CannibalismEnd
---
<<gathervars>>
<<set $NikoDiaImage = true>>
Niko: "Misery made me a wretch."
<<set $NikoDiaImage = false>>

He sliced into a peach.

Juice ran down his fingers.

He licked them clean.

Fruits lay across the table.

Apples. Pomegranates. Peaches.

<<set $NikoDiaImage = true>>
Niko: "Misery made me a wretch."
<<set $NikoDiaImage = false>>

<<set $NikoDiaImage = true>>
Niko: "But I won't let it consume me."
<<set $NikoDiaImage = false>>

He tore a pomegranate apart.

Seeds scattered like blood.

<<set $NikoDiaImage = true>>
Niko: "I admired Frankenstein once."
<<set $NikoDiaImage = false>>

<<set $NikoDiaImage = true>>
Niko: "But he abandoned his creation."
<<set $NikoDiaImage = false>>

<<set $NikoDiaImage = true>>
Niko: "I will not abandon you."
<<set $NikoDiaImage = false>>

<<set $NikoDiaImage = true>>
Niko: "You'll always be a part of me."
<<set $NikoDiaImage = false>>
<<gameFinished>>
===

title: StockholmSyndromeEndPart
---
<<gathervars>>
You: "You're more myself than I."

<<set $NikoDiaImage = true>>
Niko: "You know Wuthering Heights well."
<<set $NikoDiaImage = false>>

<<set $NikoDiaImage = true>>
Niko: "But that's not quite right."
<<set $NikoDiaImage = false>>

You: "I know."

You: "I'm speaking of us."

You: "Our souls are intertwined."

You reached for him.

His hair was soft beneath your fingers.

You: "I want to stay with you."

You: "If you'll have me?"

<<set $NikoDiaImage = true>>
Niko: "I'll have only you."
<<set $NikoDiaImage = false>>

He embraced you.

<<set $NikoDiaImage = true>>
Niko: "We will be together now."
<<set $NikoDiaImage = false>>

<<set $NikoDiaImage = true>>
Niko: "You'll always be a part of me."
<<set $NikoDiaImage = false>>

<<set $NikoDiaImage = true>>
Niko: "My soul."
<<set $NikoDiaImage = false>>
<<gameFinished>>
===

title: Graduation
---

<<gathervars>>
After everything this year, you did it. You scraped your grade
together enough to graduate!

As others threw their hats in the air, you held onto yours,
preferring something solid. A reminder that even when things
were rough, you still made it.

<<gameFinished>>
===

title: GraduationWithFaust
---
<<gathervars>>
After everything this year, you did it. You scraped your grade
together enough to graduate!

As others threw their hats in the air, you held onto yours,
preferring something solid. A reminder that even when things
were rough, you still made it.
<<moodSwitch>>
<<jump GoodFaust>>
===

title: GoodNiko
---
<<gathervars>>
Birds tweet softly as a summer breeze moves the trees outside.
Swallows loop across the blue sky beyond the locked window.
<<set $NikoDiaImage = true>>
Niko: "Are you admiring the birds, my dove?" He approaches
quietly.

Niko: "You look breathtaking,"

You are dressed carefully, styled exactly how he likes. To him,
you are delicate. Precious.

His dove. His dove in a gilded cage.

Niko: "Don't you like it?" He gestures to the table.

Croissants, pain au chocolat, and pastries cover it.

Niko: "I wanted you to feel like you were in Paris, dining
beside La Seine."

Niko: "Because, ma chérie, you deserve the best,"

He lifts your hand, kissing each knuckle slowly. A quiet
reminder of who you belong to.

He listens to distant church bells.

Niko: "Isn't today your graduation?" He tilts his head.

You: "It was. I forgot about it,"

He smiles brightly.

Niko: "An éclair?" He offers it gently.

You: "Could we go for a walk today?" You miss the outside air.

He sets the éclair down, displeased.

Niko: "I can open the window. It might feel like a walk by a
river."

Niko: "You know why you can't go out,"

He stands, kissing your forehead.

Niko: "It's alright. We all make mistakes,"

He cracks the window open slightly, the key resting around his
neck.

Niko: "It's a beautiful day,"

You smile. You agree. It is a beautiful day.
<<set $NikoDiaImage = false>>

And maybe this isn't so bad. What more could you need?...
<<gameFinished>>
===

title: GoodFaust
---
<<gathervars>>
You stop by the cafe for one last campus coffee when Faust
approaches you.
<<set $FaustDiaImage = true>>
Faust: "Those answers I gave you? Most of them were lies."

You stare at him as he looks away, shifting.

Faust: "I cared too much about how I looked. Even answering
your questions felt...wrong."

He hesitates.

Faust: "I didn't want to seem weak. So I lied."
<<set $FaustDiaImage = false>>
Silence lingers between you, and you had nothing more to say...
<<gameFinished>>
===

title: SalemEndingStart
---
<<gathervars>>
A dreadful feeling consumed you.

The need to find Salem gnawed at your mind.

Mumbling to yourself, you made a split decision to visit her.

On your way to her dorm, something flickered in your vision.

It looked distorted. Glitching.

You turned quickly, but everything looked normal again.

Your heart pounded.

The feeling of being watched crawled over your skin.

Salem: "Find me,"

Your thoughts dulled.

Your body moved on its own, drawn forward.

Panic vanished, replaced by a single purpose.

Find her.
<<jump AtTheRift>>
===

title: AtTheRift
---
<<gathervars>>
The scene before you was unlike anything you'd seen.

A dark space stretched endlessly.

A rocky hill led up to a dim blue light.

Whispers filled your ears, speaking truths you couldn't grasp.

Your mind blocked them out.

Something pushed you forward.

And so, you walked.

'Why am I walking?' you thought.

It didn't matter.

Your autonomy felt stripped away.

Your thoughts weren't your own.

Your body wasn't your own.

You climbed the hill, stones crunching beneath your feet.

At the top stood an archway.

A gate, glowing with an unnatural blue.

Dust swirled around it, shimmering in the air.

It felt wrong. Like it didn't belong.

It towered over you, large enough to swallow you whole.

The whispers urged you closer.

Then—

You saw her.
<<set $SalemDiaImage = true>>

Your trance shattered.

The whispers vanished.

You gasped.

She was here.

You rushed forward, stumbling over rocks.

Your footsteps echoed.

She turned.

Salem: "{$playerName}..."
Salem: "You came!"

Her voice echoed through the space.

Her pupils were blown wide.

She swayed, an unnatural smile stretching across her face.

You slowed, unease settling deep in your chest.

Something wasn't right.

Salem: "You came... I'm so happy..."
Salem: "You were the only one who cared..."
Salem: "Thank you... I'm so happy you're here..."

She drifted toward you like a ghost.

You: "Salem..."
You: "What are you doing here?"

Salem: "Silly {$playerName}..."
Salem: "I'm about to witness a new dream,"

She sighed happily, eyes closing.

Salem: "All my sadness will disappear there,"

Her eyes snapped open.

Salem: "It will be beautiful...!"
Salem: "A new slate... a fresh start..."
Salem: "Hehehe... HEHEHEHE..."

She grabbed your arms tightly.

It hurt.

Salem: "I'm so tired of this dream..."
Salem: "So much hate... so much sadness..."
Salem: "I want a happy dream..."

She paused.

Salem: "You're happy for me... right?"

You frowned.

You: "Don't do it."

She stared at you blankly.

Salem: "What...?"

You: "You want a new dream?"
You: "Won't you miss your friends? Your family?"
You: "Your new world won't have them. Or me."

You softened your tone.

You: "Life is harsh, but that's what makes it matter."
You: "The sun... food... laughter..."

Salem stood still.

Then she sniffled.

Tears fell.

Salem: "I'm so tired..."
Salem: "Why is everything so cruel?"
Salem: "Why do people hate...?"

She sobbed.

You pulled her into a hug.

Salem: "I don't want to feel anymore..."

You: "I know."

You held her as she cried.

You: "Come on... let's leave."

She looked up, then nodded weakly.

Together, you walked away.
<<set $SalemDiaImage = false>>

One last glance at the gate silenced the whispers for good.
<<gameFinished>>
===